e FileCount:1} {Key:redesign-existing-projects Name:redesign-existing-projects Description:Upgrades existing websites and apps to premium quality. Audits current design, identifies generic AI patterns, and applies high-end design standards without breaking functionality. Works with any CSS framework or vanilla CSS. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/redesign-existing-projects Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:research Name:research Description:Investigate a question against high-trust primary sources and capture the findings as a Markdown file in the repo. Use when the user wants a topic researched, docs or API facts gathered, or reading legwork delegated to a background agent. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/research Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:resolving-merge-conflicts Name:resolving-merge-conflicts Description:Use when you need to resolve an in-progress git merge/rebase conflict. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/resolving-merge-conflicts Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:retro Name:retro Description:Conduct a retrospective on a coding session. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/retro Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:scaffold-exercises Name:scaffold-exercises Description:Create exercise directory structures with sections, problems, solutions, and explainers that pass linting. Use when user wants to scaffold exercises, create exercise stubs, or set up a new course section. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/scaffold-exercises Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:semantic-compression Name:semantic-compression Description:Re-encode verbose prose into a dense telegraphic register — punctuation as connectives, label frames, verbless assertions — without losing normativity or precision. Use when compressing system prompts, tool/function descriptions, skill bodies, or agent instructions; reducing token count or context bloat; making documentation token-efficient for LLM input; or rewriting text in compressed notation. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/semantic-compression Provider:codebuddy Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:setup-matt-pocock-skills Name:setup-matt-pocock-skills Description:Configure this repo for the engineering skills: set up its issue tracker, triage label vocabulary, and domain doc layout. Run once before first use of the other engineering skills. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/setup-matt-pocock-skills Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:setup-pre-commit Name:setup-pre-commit Description:Set up Husky pre-commit hooks with lint-staged (Prettier), type checking, and tests in the current repo. Use when user wants to add pre-commit hooks, set up Husky, configure lint-staged, or add commit-time formatting/typechecking/testing. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/setup-pre-commit Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:setup-ts-deep-modules Name:setup-ts-deep-modules Description:Wire dependency-cruiser into a TypeScript repo so each package is a deep module, with implementation hidden in subfolders and reachable only through its entry-point files. User-invoked. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/setup-ts-deep-modules Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:stitch-design-taste Name:stitch-design-taste Description:Semantic Design System Skill for Google Stitch. Generates agent-friendly DESIGN.md files that enforce premium, anti-generic UI standards — strict typography, calibrated color, asymmetric layouts, perpetual micro-motion, and hardware-accelerated performance. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/stitch-design-taste Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:system-prompts Name:system-prompts Description:Write system prompts, tool docs, and agent definitions. Project tag conventions + RFC 2119 keywords + dense compression. Use when authoring or editing any prompt the model reads. SourcePath:~/.agents/skills/system-prompts Provider:codebuddy Root:universal Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:2} {Key:systematic-debugging Name:systematic-debugging Description:Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/systematic-debugging Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:tavily-search Name:tavily-search Description:Search the web with LLM-optimized results via the Tavily CLI. Use this skill when the user wants to search the web, find articles, look up information, get recent news, discover sources, or says "search for", "find me", "look up", "what's the latest on", "find articles about", or needs current information from the internet. Returns relevant results with content snippets, relevance scores, and metadata — optimized for LLM consumption. Supports domain filtering, time ranges, and multiple search depths. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/tavily-search Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:tdd Name:tdd Description:Test-driven development. Use when the user wants to build features or fix bugs test-first, mentions "red-green-refactor", or wants integration tests. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/tdd Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:teach Name:teach Description:Teach the user a new skill or concept, within this workspace. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/teach Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:to-questionnaire Name:to-questionnaire Description:Turn a decision you can't fully answer into a questionnaire for someone else to fill in. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/to-questionnaire Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:to-spec Name:to-spec Description:Turn the current conversation into a spec and publish it to the project issue tracker: no interview, just synthesis of what you've already discussed. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/to-spec Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:to-tickets Name:to-tickets Description:Break a plan, spec, or the current conversation into a set of tracer-bullet tickets, each declaring its blocking edges, published to the configured tracker (edges as text in one file per ticket locally, or native blocking links on a real tracker). SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/to-tickets Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:triage Name:triage Description:Move issues and external PRs through a state machine of triage roles, categorise, verify, grill if needed, and write agent-ready briefs. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/triage Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:wait-what Name:wait-what Description:Stop. That last message did not land: re-pitch it. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/wait-what Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:wayfinder Name:wayfinder Description:Plan a huge chunk of work (more than one agent session can hold) as a shared map of decision tickets on your issue tracker, and resolve them one at a time until the way to the destination is clear. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/wayfinder Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:wizard Name:wizard Description:Generate an interactive bash wizard that walks a human through steps only they can perform. Use when provisioning infrastructure, setting up credentials or CI secrets, walking an unfamiliar third-party dashboard, or running a one-off migration or cutover. Don't invoke this for steps the agent can perform itself. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/wizard Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:writing-beats Name:writing-beats Description:Writing, exploit; assemble raw material into a journey of beats, grounding each term before a beat leans on it. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/writing-beats Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:writing-for-agents Name:writing-for-agents Description:Writing documents for agents. Use when creating or editing skills, or modifying AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/writing-for-agents Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:writing-fragments Name:writing-fragments Description:Writing, explore: mine raw fragments, no structure yet. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/writing-fragments Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:writing-plans Name:writing-plans Description:Use when you have a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/writing-plans Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1} {Key:writing-shape Name:writing-shape Description:Writing, exploit: shape raw material into an article, paragraph by paragraph. SourcePath:~/.codebuddy/skills/writing-shape Provider:codebuddy Root:provider Plugin: CanDisable:false FileCount:1}]
