andardize dates, remove duplicates, and flag mixed-type columns. Use when data is messy, inconsistent, or needs prep before analysis. Triggers on \"clean this data\", \"clean up this sheet\", \"normalize this data\", \"fix formatting\", \"dedupe\", \"standardize this column\", \"this data is messy\".", SourcePath:"~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-for-financial-services/financial-analysis/0.1.1/skills/clean-data-xls", Provider:"claude", Root:"plugin", Plugin:"financial-analysis@claude-for-financial-services", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"financial-analysis:competitive-analysis", Name:"financial-analysis:competitive-analysis", Description:"Framework for building competitive landscape decks — market positioning, competitor deep-dives, comparative analysis, strategic synthesis. Use when the user asks for a competitive landscape, competitor analysis, peer comparison, market positioning assessment, strategic review, or investment memo deck. Also triggers on \"who are the competitors to X\", \"benchmark X against peers\", \"build a market map\", or any request to systematically evaluate competitive dynamics across an industry.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-for-financial-services/financial-analysis/0.1.1/skills/competitive-analysis", Provider:"claude", Root:"plugin", Plugin:"financial-analysis@claude-for-financial-services", CanDisable:true, FileCount:3}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"financial-analysis:comps-analysis", Name:"financial-analysis:comps-analysis", Description:"Build institutional-grade comparable company analyses with operating metrics, valuation multiples, and statistical benchmarking in Excel/spreadsheet format.\n\n**Perfect for:**\n- Public company valuation (M&A, investment analysis)\n- Benchmarking performance vs. industry peers\n- Pricing IPOs or funding rounds\n- Identifying valuation outliers (over/under-valued)\n- Supporting investment committee presentations\n- Creating sector overview reports\n\n**Not ideal for:**\n- Private companies without comparable public peers\n- Highly diversified conglomerates\n- Distressed/bankrupt companies\n- Pre-revenue startups\n- Companies with unique business models", SourcePath:"~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-for-financial-services/financial-analysis/0.1.1/skills/comps-analysis", Provider:"claude", Root:"plugin", Plugin:"financial-analysis@claude-for-financial-services", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"financial-analysis:dcf-model", Name:"financial-analysis:dcf-model", Description:"Real DCF (Discounted Cash Flow) model creation for equity valuation. Retrieves financial data from SEC filings and analyst reports, builds comprehensive cash flow projections with proper WACC calculations, performs sensitivity analysis, and outputs professional Excel models with executive summaries. Use when users need to value a company using DCF methodology, request intrinsic value analysis, or ask for detailed financial modeling with growth projections and terminal value calculations.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-for-financial-services/financial-analysis/0.1.1/skills/dcf-model", Provider:"claude", Root:"plugin", Plugin:"financial-analysis@claude-for-financial-services", CanDisable:true, FileCount:4}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"financial-analysis:deck-refresh", Name:"financial-analysis:deck-refresh", Description:"Updates a presentation with new numbers — quarterly refreshes, earnings updates, comp rolls, rebased market data. Use whenever the user asks to \"update the deck with Q4 numbers\", \"refresh the comps\", \"roll this forward\", \"swap in the new earnings\", \"change all the $485M to $512M\", or any request to swap figures across an existing deck without rebuilding it.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-for-financial-services/financial-analysis/0.1.1/skills/deck-refresh", Provider:"claude", Root:"plugin", Plugin:"financial-analysis@claude-for-financial-services", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"financial-analysis:ib-check-deck", Name:"financial-analysis:ib-check-deck", Description:"Investment banking presentation quality checker. Reviews a pitch deck or client-ready presentation for (1) number consistency across slides, (2) data-narrative alignment, (3) language polish against IB standards, (4) visual and formatting QC. Use whenever the user asks to review, check, QC, proof, or do a final pass on a deck, pitch, or client materials — including requests like \"check my numbers\", \"reconcile figures across slides\", \"is this client-ready\", or \"what am I missing before I send this out\".", SourcePath:"~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-for-financial-services/financial-analysis/0.1.1/skills/ib-check-deck", Provider:"claude", Root:"plugin", Plugin:"financial-analysis@claude-for-financial-services", CanDisable:true, FileCount:4}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"financial-analysis:lbo-model", Name:"financial-analysis:lbo-model", Description:"This skill should be used when completing LBO (Leveraged Buyout) model templates in Excel for private equity transactions, deal materials, or investment committee presentations. The skill fills in formulas, validates calculations, and ensures professional formatting standards that adapt to any template structure.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-for-financial-services/financial-analysis/0.1.1/skills/lbo-model", Provider:"claude", Root:"plugin", Plugin:"financial-analysis@claude-for-financial-services", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"financial-analysis:ppt-template-creator", Name:"financial-analysis:ppt-template-creator", Description:"Creates self-contained PPT template SKILLS (not presentations) from user-provided PowerPoint templates. Use ONLY when a user wants to create a reusable skill from their template. For creating actual presentations, use the pptx skill instead.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-for-financial-services/financial-analysis/0.1.1/skills/ppt-template-creator", Provider:"claude", Root:"plugin", Plugin:"financial-analysis@claude-for-financial-services", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"financial-analysis:pptx-author", Name:"financial-analysis:pptx-author", Description:"Produce a .pptx file on disk (headless) instead of driving a live PowerPoint document — for managed-agent sessions with no open Office app.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-for-financial-services/financial-analysis/0.1.1/skills/pptx-author", Provider:"claude", Root:"plugin", Plugin:"financial-analysis@claude-for-financial-services", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"financial-analysis:skill-creator", Name:"financial-analysis:skill-creator", Description:"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claude's capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-for-financial-services/financial-analysis/0.1.1/skills/skill-creator", Provider:"claude", Root:"plugin", Plugin:"financial-analysis@claude-for-financial-services", CanDisable:true, FileCount:6}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"financial-analysis:xlsx-author", Name:"financial-analysis:xlsx-author", Description:"Produce a .xlsx file on disk (headless) instead of driving a live Excel workbook — for managed-agent sessions with no open Office app.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-for-financial-services/financial-analysis/0.1.1/skills/xlsx-author", Provider:"claude", Root:"plugin", Plugin:"financial-analysis@claude-for-financial-services", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"finishing-a-development-branch", Name:"finishing-a-development-branch", Description:"Use when implementation is complete, all tests pass, and you need to decide how to integrate the work", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/finishing-a-development-branch", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"full-output-enforcement", Name:"full-output-enforcement", Description:"Overrides default LLM truncation behavior. Enforces complete code generation, bans placeholder patterns, and handles token-limit splits cleanly. Apply to any task requiring exhaustive, unabridged output.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/full-output-enforcement", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"git-guardrails-claude-code", Name:"git-guardrails-claude-code", Description:"Set up Claude Code hooks to block dangerous git commands (push, reset --hard, clean, branch -D, etc.) before they execute. Use when user wants to prevent destructive git operations, add git safety hooks, or block git push/reset in Claude Code.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/git-guardrails-claude-code", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"gpt-taste", Name:"gpt-taste", Description:"Elite UX/UI & Advanced GSAP Motion Engineer. Enforces Python-driven true randomization for layout variance, strict AIDA page structure, wide editorial typography (bans 6-line wraps), gapless bento grids, strict GSAP ScrollTriggers (pinning, stacking, scrubbing), inline micro-images, and massive section spacing.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/gpt-taste", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"graphify", Name:"graphify-windows", Description:"Use for any question about a codebase, its architecture, file relationships, or project content — especially when graphify-out/ exists, where the question should be treated as a graphify query first. Turns any input (code, docs, papers, images, videos) into a persistent knowledge graph with god nodes, community detection, and query/path/explain tools.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/graphify", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:9}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"grill-me", Name:"grill-me", Description:"A relentless interview to sharpen a plan or design.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/grill-me", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"grill-with-docs", Name:"grill-with-docs", Description:"A relentless interview to sharpen a plan or design, which also creates docs (ADR's and glossary) as we go.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/grill-with-docs", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"grilling", Name:"grilling", Description:"Grill the user relentlessly about a plan, decision, or idea. Use when the user wants to stress-test their thinking, or uses any 'grill' trigger phrases.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/grilling", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"handoff", Name:"handoff", Description:"Compact the current conversation into a handoff document for another agent to pick up.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/handoff", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"high-end-visual-design", Name:"high-end-visual-design", Description:"Teaches the AI to design like a high-end agency. Defines the exact fonts, spacing, shadows, card structures, and animations that make a website feel expensive. Blocks all the common defaults that make AI designs look cheap or generic.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/high-end-visual-design", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"image-to-code", Name:"image-to-code", Description:"Elite website image-to-code skill for Codex. For visually important web tasks, it must first generate the design image(s) itself, deeply analyze them, then implement the website to match them as closely as possible. In Codex, it must prefer large, readable, section-specific images instead of tiny compressed boards, generate fresh standalone images for sections or detail views instead of cropping old ones, avoid lazy under-generation, avoid cards-inside-cards-inside-cards UI, and keep the hero clean, spacious, readable, and visible on a small laptop.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/image-to-code", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"imagegen-frontend-mobile", Name:"imagegen-frontend-mobile", Description:"Elite mobile app image-generation skill for creating premium, app-native screen concepts and flows. Designed for iOS, Android, and cross-platform mobile products. Prioritizes clean hierarchy, comfortably readable text, strong multi-screen consistency, controlled color palettes, non-generic creative direction, textured surfaces, image-led composition, tasteful custom iconography, and clean phone mockup framing. By default, screens should be shown inside a subtle premium iPhone or similar phone mockup with a visible frame, while the main focus stays on the app content itself. This skill generates images only. It does not write code.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/imagegen-frontend-mobile", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"imagegen-frontend-web", Name:"imagegen-frontend-web", Description:"Elite frontend image-direction skill for generating premium, conversion-aware website design references. CRITICAL OUTPUT RULE — generate ONE separate horizontal image FOR EVERY section. A landing page with 8 sections produces 8 images. Never compress multiple sections into one image. Enforces composition variety (not always left-text / right-image), background-image freedom, varied CTAs, varied hero scales (giant / mid / mini minimalist), narrative concept spine, second-read moments, and a single consistent palette across all images. Optimized for landing pages, marketing sites, and product comps that developers or coding models can accurately recreate.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/imagegen-frontend-web", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"implement", Name:"implement", Description:"Implement a piece of work based on a spec or set of tickets.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/implement", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"implement-spec", Name:"implement-spec", Description:"Implement a specification in code.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/implement-spec", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"improve-codebase-architecture", Name:"improve-codebase-architecture", Description:"Scan a codebase for deepening opportunities, present them as a visual HTML report, then grill through whichever one you pick.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/improve-codebase-architecture", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"industrial-brutalist-ui", Name:"industrial-brutalist-ui", Description:"Raw mechanical interfaces fusing Swiss typographic print with military terminal aesthetics. Rigid grids, extreme type scale contrast, utilitarian color, analog degradation effects. For data-heavy dashboards, portfolios, or editorial sites that need to feel like declassified blueprints.", SourcePath:"~/.claude/skills/industrial-brutalist-ui", Provider:"claude", Root:"provider", Plugin:"", CanDisable:true, FileCount:1}, daemon.runtimeLocalSkillSummary{Key:"jev-ultrafast", Name:"jev-ultrafast", Description:"", SourcePath:"~/.agents/skills/jev-ultrafast", Provider:"clau